 with 11 h 9 m of daylight. Since 6:00 AM at North Island, no rain; air 67\u201371 \u00b0F (19\u201322 \u00b0C) and humidity 57\u201371%, 70 \u00b0F (21 \u00b0C) and 59% at 10:52 AM. Water 75 \u00b0F (23.8 \u00b0C) at CDIP 191."],["Swell","CDIP 191 at 11:00 AM: 14.3 s from SSW 205\u00b0, 2.9 ft (0.89 m); 9.1 s from W 266\u00b0, 1.8 ft (0.56 m); wind sea 4.3 s from WNW 284\u00b0, 1.4 ft (0.42 m). At 5:00 AM: 14.3 s from S 182\u00b0, 2.8 ft (0.84 m); 9.9 s from W 280\u00b0, 2.3 ft (0.71 m); wind sea 4.2 s from W 277\u00b0, 1.8 ft (0.54 m). Breaking at 11:00 AM, against 5:00 AM: North 3.6 ft (1.10 m), little change; Center 2.8 ft (0.86 m), little change; South 2.8 ft (0.85 m), little change. North leads. Coming: west swell (250\u2013280\u00b0) rose at Tanner Banks (NDBC 46047) from 7:07 AM, 10\u201312 s first; by deep-water speed it is due at CDIP 191 around 1:32 PM, at the breaks 39\u201353 min after. Due, not seen."],["Tide","The tide is dropping to 2.8 ft (0.85 m) at 1:33 PM then pushing to 6.2 ft (1.90 m) at 7:26 PM. The previous AM high was 6.5 ft (1.97 m) at 7:31 AM. The gauge is running 1.5 ft (0.46 m) over the harmonic prediction, over the last 3 days. Today's range is 4.4 ft (1.34 m), building toward springs; springs around Oct 25. On the 2016 survey the tide moves where the waves break, not how big they are; this season's sandbars are not known."],["Wind","WSW 250\u00b0 at 3 mph (3 kt) at 10:52 AM: light onshore at all three breaks. At this hour on the 33 days before: North light or variable on 10, onshore on 12; Center light or variable on 10, onshore on 13; South light or variable on 10, onshore on 17. Median 7 mph (6 kt)."],["Watching","Former hurricane [Trudy](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/archive/2026/TRUDY_graphics.php): every fix NHC has logged or forecast is behind land from Point Loma South, so nothing it has sent reaches the breaks."]]}}